{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787175152388710001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"seraphic-taming-terrier","assignee":null,"attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"sshsig","author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","envelope":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.opcert.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","head_sha":"0b851c81032aa1a2032296848b4e091d171abb34","key_id":null,"kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: 3ed6-b264-e1ae-41a0","material: 4d8f0ca81ba06bbf","material-part: children 647ea2107ca5072f 0","material-part: description 1bbef087e37ff6e3 3129","material-part: description_boxes 6c179f21e6f62b62 0","material-part: file_impact 003ffa614d5e4a28 0","material-part: ticket_id 89d62ce9a65876b2 19","model: bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 3","review-phase: planning","rebar-version: 0.12.0 (0b851c8103)","regver: 1da3feeb7c09e17f","verified-at-sha:0b851c81032aa1a2032296848b4e091d171abb34","currency-basis: fail-safe"],"material_fingerprint":"4d8f0ca81ba06bbf","merged_log_commit":"0b851c81032aa1a2032296848b4e091d171abb34","principal":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","signature":null,"signed_at":1787169791320417000}},"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":7,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"238f1371113311db100d9bcc3b5d8c0e1285105236911fe3eb974c8332e77f6b","event_uuid":"9a1ef723-eaf3-4f22-9ef6-e3aebdba2690","position":{"commit_sha":"1ba378e243f10e91a9d6e5a3bf412494d47f6712","position":"1787169593571050001-9a1ef723-eaf3-4f22-9ef6-e3aebdba2690"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"85de90a6cd2ef411c81081cae09ea166e4a5102b356b4c616f4e31929657a373","event_uuid":"7e67dc62-0b81-4fd8-bf2d-26cbaa19e3de","position":{"commit_sha":"331f63d48aee2c8dd4eb35b9831da5dd97789ce5","position":"1787169603606481001-7e67dc62-0b81-4fd8-bf2d-26cbaa19e3de"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8032f74f16bbd3d6095cf9359b7f0f9113926297307fc2103ab6acf7c6f76057","event_uuid":"da8cd979-6585-4bb5-8375-41edec1d14fd","position":{"commit_sha":"c2f07acabf539e92e9b11754adb06ef45ecfd963","position":"1787169609294640001-da8cd979-6585-4bb5-8375-41edec1d14fd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5768fc576a09f183b80abebc043a51e1e31145663cc899f70e2906d6b8ef0592","event_uuid":"bd3a665e-040f-4715-8029-cae5eaf845fe","position":{"commit_sha":"cd6cfede654c9c234c68f16353c3a3279173e208","position":"1787169791339389001-bd3a665e-040f-4715-8029-cae5eaf845fe"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3b100d56f2e6eb70978e30d248092ed19557fa0d3189b5bad152bbf78ceef2a9","event_uuid":"51dd2b17-96a3-4539-bb94-270d26852de6","position":{"commit_sha":"f7b6ea4413133ba8f277722695ef27d0018bb925","position":"1787170361436086001-51dd2b17-96a3-4539-bb94-270d26852de6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"62dde8b18e97eed0284994c7bba52639e337417a712c0bba58906dc258d09781","event_uuid":"cfdfc64a-0790-47ea-9cf8-f8b7119a1b3d","position":{"commit_sha":"3fd2c224cf1cef91a0ebc5f0b67c9ddebc44b75c","position":"1787170464181223001-cfdfc64a-0790-47ea-9cf8-f8b7119a1b3d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9feccddde79518c4e815dd141817a68e45d3d907bdcc7f2110f3315a438757cd","event_uuid":"62e5c422-3970-4cce-9af3-2f2cb44c07d2","position":{"commit_sha":"49f145f759fd78250858018834442a9c62ebc023","position":"1787170654307500001-62e5c422-3970-4cce-9af3-2f2cb44c07d2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## /rebar-debug RCA — mechanism PROVEN; legitimacy classified NOT-A-BUG (feature-request). No fix applied.\n\nInvestigated at origin/main `0b851c8103` in an isolated worktree. Phase 1 completed; the Phase-2\nnot-a-bug guard held, so **no code change was made** and the disposition is handed to a human.\n\n### Proven mechanism (confirmed by runtime measurement, not by reading source)\n\nA gate op is a multi-phase pipeline; **no component emits anything between command start and the\nfinal verdict at the default log level**. Three contributing facts, all confirmed:\n\n1. **The two longest phases have NO instrumentation at any level.** Measured at\n   `REBAR_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG` (rebar's most verbose setting) on `review-plan --force`, total 130.4s:\n   - `t+0 -> t+27.1` = **27.1s** silent — material-assembly / store-hydration prologue.\n   - `t+52.2 -> t+92.2` = **40.0s** silent — overlap-corpus retrieval\n     (`overlap corpus: 852 fresh digests, 3833 skipped`). Pure LOCAL compute, no model call.\n2. **The phase logs that do exist are INFO and fire AFTER their phase completes**, never at its\n   start: `llm/plan_review/pass1.py:274`, `llm/workflow/container_stage.py:189,235,290`,\n   `llm/agent_call.py:381`. The default level is WARNING (`_logging.py:_resolve_level`, :91-100),\n   overridable only by `REBAR_LOG_LEVEL` — there is no `--verbose` that raises it.\n3. **The sole shared LLM seam emits nothing during the call.** Every gate op funnels through\n   `PydanticAIRunner.run` (`llm/runner.py:296`); the leaves are non-streaming\n   `agent.run_sync` (`llm/runner.py:540`, `llm/structured_run.py:211`, `:249`). `run_stream` has\n   NEVER existed in `src/rebar/llm/` (`git log -S'run_stream'` => zero commits).\n\n### Discriminating experiments (3 runs, same worktree/ticket)\n\n| run | level | LLM | silent prologue | largest later gap | total |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | WARNING (default) | fresh | 54.2s | **85.4s** to verdict | 146.9s |\n| 2 | DEBUG | none (reuse path) | 27.2s | — | 27.4s |\n| 3 | DEBUG | forced fresh | 27.1s | **40.0s** (overlap retrieval) | 130.4s |\n\n- Run 1 vs Run 3 **rejects** \"the signals exist but sit below the default level\": raising the level\n  reveals per-call lines, yet 27s and 40s holes remain, so those phases have nothing to suppress.\n- Run 2 **rejects** \"the silence is the model call\": it made no model call and was still silent for\n  27.2s (11.9s user + 13.0s system of real work).\n- Run 1's own verdict reports `llm_ms: 13047` of a **146,900 ms** wall clock — the model is ~9% of\n  the run. A streaming-only remedy (the ticket's remedy #2) would therefore NOT break the failure.\n\nEmission plumbing is NOT the gap: run 1's three `enrich_drain` WARNINGs arrived through a pipe\n85s before exit, proving `logging`->stderr already flushes promptly mid-run. Nothing chooses to write.\n\n### Legitimacy: `feature-request` — cited, and this is why no fix was applied\n\nProgress emission on gate ops was never built and never removed (not a regression). The\nlong-silent-run behaviour is, by contrast, **deliberate and recorded twice**:\n\n- **ADR 0089 — \"Activity-based liveness under run_sync; async idle-watchdog deferred\"** (Accepted\n  2026-07-09, ~1 month old, so it states CURRENT intent): LLM gate runs' *\"time-to-first-token can\n  legitimately be minutes of silence\"*; *\"No total-runtime timeout anywhere in the gate path\"*; the\n  reset-on-event stream watchdog *\"is NOT built\"*, deferred behind a stated trigger (migrating the\n  runner to async `agent.run()`), which is unmet. Restated at `docs/config.md:402-406`.\n- **`docs/plan-review-gate.md:1415-1424`, section \"End-to-end time-to-first-work (honest)\"**: the\n  review *\"takes seconds to minutes depending on ticket size + tier\"* and *\"no upfront wall-clock\n  benchmark is claimed\"* — a deliberate refusal, which is what AC-2 of this ticket asks to reverse.\n\nNo doc, test, or contract requires a gate op to emit progress or bound its silence. Under the\nprotocol's three-way test this is \"never built, and nothing shows it was designed\" =>\n**feature-request**, which is fail-closed: a human decides, rather than an agent patching it in.\n\n### Honest counter-argument (why this is not a slam dunk)\n\nADR 0089's subject is INBOUND liveness — how rebar bounds a hung *model*. It never posed the\noutbound question \"should rebar announce it is alive?\" And its \"time-to-first-token\" justification\ndoes not reach the two dominant holes, which are **local compute** (27s prologue, 40s overlap\nretrieval) with no recorded justification at all. A reviewer could fairly read those two phases as\nan unjustified gap rather than an intended design. That is the strongest case for `defect`; it did\nnot clear the bar of a *cited* authoritative source, so the guard held.\n\n### Recommended disposition (for a human to accept or reject)\n\n1. **Cheapest effective remedy, and ADR 0089 does NOT block it.** The ADR deferred a *stream-event\n   idle watchdog* (kills a stalled run; needs async). A *periodic liveness emitter* is a different\n   mechanism and is already proven compatible with blocking sync code in this repo:\n   `_engine/rebar_reconciler/_heartbeat.py:52-93` runs `threading.Thread(daemon=True)` +\n   `stop.wait(interval)`. A ~30s heartbeat to stderr wrapping the gate op would break the failure.\n   Natural seams, coarse to fine: `llm/workflow/executor.py:641` (per workflow step),\n   `llm/runner.py:296` (per LLM call), `llm/agent_call.py:178,202` (per tool call).\n   Constraint: `src/rebar/llm/**` is NOT on the ruff T201 print allowlist (`pyproject.toml:399-440`),\n   so it must go through `logging`, not `print`.\n2. **Re-scope AC-2.** It asks docs to state an expected duration range, but\n   `docs/plan-review-gate.md:1420-1424` deliberately declines to claim a benchmark. The\n   defensible doc change is not a benchmark but a **warning that gate ops routinely exceed common\n   600s supervisor stall budgets while silent**, plus how to raise them. Note `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_S`\n   is itself `600` (`llm/config.py:124`) *per request*, and the close path can issue many requests\n   (`close_autoresume.py:191` is a `while True` up to `verify.auto_resume_max`), so worst-case\n   wall clock is a large multiple of the very budget that killed the reporting agent.\n3. If accepted, this should be re-typed from `bug` to a feature/task and given acceptance criteria\n   naming a proving command, per the advisory findings its own plan review returned (P1/P9/P10).\n\nNo files were changed. Worktree retired.","timestamp":1787170361436086001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"### Addendum — an EXISTING TEST pins the inverse, and any future fix must not break it\n\nA second independent pass confirmed the three findings above (no `run_stream`/`stream_events`/\n`isatty` commit has ever touched `src/rebar/llm/`; ADR 0089 governs; no prior ticket) and found one\ncitation I had missed that **strengthens** the not-a-bug classification rather than weakening it:\n\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py:367` — `test_no_total_runtime_timer_mechanism`\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py:181` — `test_slow_but_alive_server_completes_under_read_timeout`\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py:256` — `test_sync_tool_is_not_interrupted_documented_caveat`\n\nThese assert that a slow-but-alive run completes and that no total-runtime timer exists — i.e. the\ntest suite **pins silence-tolerance as correct behaviour**. So the authoritative record does not\nmerely fail to require progress output; it affirmatively encodes the opposite. That is a hard\nconstraint on any future implementation: a progress heartbeat must be **purely additive emission**\nand must not introduce a total-runtime cap or otherwise truncate a healthy long run, or it will\nfail these tests and contradict ADR 0089.\n\nRejected as authority (checked, not applicable): the `silent`/`silently` language in\n`docs/llm-framework.md:336` and `docs/plan-review-gate.md:184,1101` means *semantically* silent\n(dropping a finding unrecorded), not output silence; all heartbeat/watchdog machinery in\n`docs/concurrency.md:240`, `docs/config.md:312` and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/` belongs to\nthe reconciler ref-lock lease and the CI bridge canary, a different subsystem that never touches the\nLLM gate path; and `tests/unit/workflow/test_executor.py:183-192` (\"progress marker\") asserts an\nin-memory `MemoryRecorder` step status for status polling, not stderr output.\n\nCorroborating field note: open session_log `bane-coach-golly` (`003a-09ae-9983-4007`) records that\nrunning pass1 with `REBAR_LOG_LEVEL=INFO` \"made the 'hang' legible\" — independently reproducing this\ninvestigation's run-1-vs-run-3 result, and confirming that the only existing mitigation is the\nopt-in log level, not a duplicate ticket.","timestamp":1787170464181223001}],"created_at":1787169593571050001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7e67dc62-0b81-4fd8-bf2d-26cbaa19e3de","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036"},{"link_uuid":"da8cd979-6585-4bb5-8375-41edec1d14fd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"08c8-2236-376f-435e"}],"description":"## Symptom\nAn autonomous agent orchestrating rebar was KILLED mid-close by its harness: `Agent stalled: no progress for 600s (stream watchdog did not recover)`. It died immediately after reporting it was auditing residual gaps for an epic close — i.e. at the point it would have invoked a close / `verify-completion` / `review-plan` gate. All nine of its code changes had already landed; the epic and one story were left stranded `in_progress` with every descendant closed, requiring a separate session to finish the two transitions.\n\n## Mechanism\nrebar's LLM gate operations (`transition ... closed` with the completion-verification gate enabled, `review-plan`, `verify-completion`) run a single long model call and emit NOTHING to stdout/stderr between start and final verdict. Measured in this session:\n\n- `rebar transition <story> in_progress closed` — exceeded a 600s foreground timeout, then ran to completion in the background. Total output before the final `transitioned ...` line: three unrelated `enrich_drain` warnings and one build-drift advisory. No progress indication for the duration.\n- `rebar review-plan <epic>` — same shape, still producing no output minutes in.\n\nAny supervisor that treats \"no output\" as \"no progress\" therefore cannot distinguish a healthy 10-minute gate call from a hung process, and will kill a correct run. This is not specific to one harness: a 600s silence budget is an ordinary default.\n\n## Why this is rebar's problem, not only the supervisor's\nThe gates are the sanctioned, documented path for claiming and closing work (AGENTS.md requires them), and closing is the LAST step of a long autonomous run — so the failure lands where the most state is at risk and the most work has already been invested. An operation that routinely runs longer than common watchdog budgets while emitting nothing is hostile to the automation rebar is explicitly designed for.\n\n## Suggested remedies (any one would break the failure)\n1. Emit periodic progress to stderr during a long gate call — even a heartbeat naming the phase (`prompt built`, `model call issued`, `awaiting verdict`, elapsed seconds).\n2. Stream or chunk the model interaction so output appears incrementally.\n3. Document the expected wall-clock range for each gate op, so operators can raise supervisor budgets deliberately rather than discovering the limit by losing a run.\n\n## Related\nDiscovered while completing epic 5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036 (citric-moudly-vipersquid) after its executor agent died this way. Distinct from bug 08c8-2236-376f-435e (frangible-irongray-adouri), which is a packaging/exit-code defect on the same close path — that one makes a crashed close look successful; this one makes a successful close look hung. They compound: a supervisor that survives the silence may then be told exit 0 by a close that never happened.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] A close/review-plan/verify-completion invocation emits at least one progress signal well inside a 600s window, on a repo where the call takes minutes.\n- [ ] The documented gate reference states the expected duration range and the interaction with supervisor stall budgets.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","08c8-2236-376f-435e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"62e5c422-3970-4cce-9af3-2f2cb44c07d2","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"idea","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3ed6-b264-e1ae-41a0","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Long-running LLM gate operations emit no incremental output, starving supervising agents' stall watchdogs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9a1ef723-eaf3-4f22-9ef6-e3aebdba2690","7e67dc62-0b81-4fd8-bf2d-26cbaa19e3de","da8cd979-6585-4bb5-8375-41edec1d14fd","bd3a665e-040f-4715-8029-cae5eaf845fe","51dd2b17-96a3-4539-bb94-270d26852de6","cfdfc64a-0790-47ea-9cf8-f8b7119a1b3d","62e5c422-3970-4cce-9af3-2f2cb44c07d2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787175152388710001,"uuid":"c39817a9-0b5c-43a7-a2c7-a0af3cc412b0"}